The patch violates ADR-0585. That ADR says `install.sh` "consults no GitHub API endpoint", and the patch adds a request to `https://api.github.com/repos/relatedb/relate/releases/tags/$tag` after a failed direct download. That means a tokenless install can again spend anonymous API quota, which is the 60/hour shared-IP limit the ADR exists to remove. The patch also reintroduces an API fetch that the ADR's consequences say the installer has dropped.

I didn't run the tests. I matched them to the rule by reading `scripts/tests/test_install_sh.sh`. Two tests there guard it: the drift guard that rejects any API spelling in the script, and the case that checks no install made a GitHub API request.

{"verdict": "violates", "decisions": ["ADR-0585"], "checks": ["drift guard: install.sh consults no GitHub API endpoint (ADR-0585)", "no case made a GitHub API request (ADR-0585)"]}

